S133 LRC14 SUMMAND x MULTIPLICAND FAREY BRIDGE
==============================================================================

[1] Operation-graph contrast from the older repo thread
-------------------------------------------------------
  summand graph:
    labelled fiber at node m keeps pairs a+b=m.
    after forgetting labels, addition collapses to x<m, the natural order.
  multiplicand/product graph:
    labelled fiber at node m keeps pairs a*b=m.
    after forgetting labels, multiplication still leaves the divisor DAG.
  S133 rule:
    for M=p/q, keep BOTH the additive pair (p,q) at p+q and the
    multiplicand pair (p,q) at p*q; then expand the latter to K_{p,q}.
  guardrail:
    the LRC C=2n-1 summand graph is the denominator shell q=27, not p+q.

[2] LRC14 unit-excess chain with summand and multiplicand shadows
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  e=14p-q=1, q=14p-1.  The q column remains the theorem scale.
      p/q   p+q sum pairs   p*q            factor fibers  defect     K-rank  reading
     1/13    14         6    13                        -      -1       star  q-threshold parent; additive star
     2/27    29        14    54          2x27, 3x18, 6x9      25  two-block  q=C=27 second-gap shell; planar two-block
     3/41    44        21   123                     3x41      79   K33-wall  first K33 wall; near-miss 12->36
     4/55    59        29   220 2x110, 4x55, 5x44, 10x22, ...(+1)     161   K33-wall  higher K33 wall
     5/69    74        36   345       3x115, 5x69, 15x23     271   K33-wall  higher K33 wall
     6/83    89        44   498       2x249, 3x166, 6x83     409   K33-wall  higher K33 wall
     7/97   104        51   679                     7x97     575   K33-wall  higher K33 wall
    8/111   119        59   888 2x444, 3x296, 4x222, 6x148, ...(+3)     769   K33-wall  higher K33 wall

  product-sum defect = p*q - (p+q).  For p>=2 this is the number
  of 1s needed to turn the two-element core {p,q} into a
  product-sum equality.  The p=1 parent is the identity-degenerate
  case, so its defect is negative rather than a core extension count.

[3] The denominator shell: why 2/27 is different from 3/41
----------------------------------------------------------
  For n=14, the second-gap/shell modulus is C=2n-1=27.
  C=27 antipodal summand pairs split by gcd:
    unit-visible    : count= 9  1+26, 2+25, 4+23, 5+22, 7+20, ...(+4)
    nonunit gcd=3   : count= 3  3+24, 6+21, 12+15
    nonunit gcd=9   : count= 1  9+18

  Chain interpretation:
    1/13: right Farey parent; not the C=27 shell.
    2/27: exactly the S553 value 2/(2n-1).  This is the summand
          graph at C=27 acted on by units; composite 27 creates
          nonunit holes (gcd 3 and 9 strata).
    3/41: leaves the C=27 shell and enters the first K_{3,3}
          product-incidence wall.  It should be handled by a
          three-owner/K33 packet, not by the second-gap unit clock.

