[5] Multiplicand graph closeup
------------------------------
  2/27: product node 54 = 2 * 3^3
    product-graph factor fibers: 2x27, 3x18, 6x9
    K_{2,27}: edges=54, rank=two-block
  3/41: product node 123 = 3 * 41
    product-graph factor fibers: 3x41
    K_{3,41}: edges=123, rank=K33-wall
  4/55: product node 220 = 2^2 * 5 * 11
    product-graph factor fibers: 2x110, 4x55, 5x44, 10x22, 11x20
    K_{4,55}: edges=220, rank=K33-wall

  Reading: the multiplicand graph and K_{p,q} are not the same object.
  The product graph records factor fibers of the integer p*q; K_{p,q}
  is the incidence blow-up of the particular fiber (p,q).  The p=2
  row has rich 3-adic product fibers but no K33 blow-up; p=3 has a
  simple product node but enough incidence rank to cross K33.

[6] Tournament Analysis on bridge carriers
------------------------------------------
  vertices considered/challenged:
    runners, gaps, denominator shells, Farey pairs, factor fibers,
    Kpq incidence blowups, K33 packets, and proof obligations.
  chosen vertices: proof carriers, not runners.
  pair observable: role score
    (theorem safety, additive shell retention, multiplicand fiber retention,
     K33 signal, LRC specificity, false-positive resistance)
  switch/gauge: lexicographically larger role score wins.
  preserves: which carrier should handle which branch of the LRC14 split.
  destroys: exact safe arcs, runner labels, and continuous phase geometry.
  fingerprint: score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1} c3=0 scc=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1) hp=1
  first Hamiltonian path: q-binding > C27-shell > Farey p+q > product fiber > Kpq blowup > K33 packet > raw apex iso
  product-only gauge would flip 9 carrier pairs.

[7] Proof readout
-----------------
  New split refined from S131:
    p=2 is not just planar.  It is the exact C=27 second-gap
    summand-unit quotient, so the right tools are HYP-2083/HYP-2161,
    petal rigidity, nonunit gcd strata, and lift/CRT conservativity.
    p>=3 is a different branch.  It starts at 3/41, where the
    denominator leaves C=27 and the K_{p,q} incidence blow-up has
    a K_{3,3} minor.  That branch should feed a finite three-owner
    obstruction packet, possibly the HYP-2908 tournament-state lift.
  Salient theorem target:
    prove every remaining q=14 non-AP/GW atom either reduces to the
    C=27 p=2 shell/petal branch or crosses the p>=3 K33 packet wall.
    Do not scalarize product fibers or apex iso classes before the
    q-shell, owner, and incidence labels have done their work.
